# AUTOMATICALLY DETERMINING POTD KIND #

I've noticed people need to keep editing the Main Page to adjust the POTD text to "Today's featured video" or "Today's featured pictures" (plural). I wrote a short module,  [LINK: (Module:POTD kind) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Module:POTD_kind] , that parses the POTD to determine what is being shown, and then returns the correct text. I've  [LINK: (updated) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Wikipedia:Main_Page/sandbox&diff=prev&oldid=1335612245]  the  [LINK: (sandbox) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Main_Page/sandbox]  to use it and in my short review of the various POTD protected pages, it seems to work correctly. And if the module doesn't work, it'll default back to "picture", so it shouldn't be any worse than the status quo (I hope).

Let me know what you think, if it's all good then I can update the real Main Page in a few days.  [LINK: (Legoktm) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Legoktm]  ( [LINK: (talk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_talk:Legoktm] )  [LINK: (05:01, 30 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Main_Page#c-Legoktm-20260130050100-Automatically_determining_POTD_kind] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Main_Page] ]

